Antencoder-AntVLA
Small VLA for Real-World Manipulation
AntVLA is a research project toward a small, deployable Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model for real-world manipulation.
The goal is not to build a model that understands everything.

Build a small model that understands enough to work.
The core idea is to represent What and How as continuous latent variables, with Language acting as a compact semantic interface.
